{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a14b6b-70c8-79b0-8bfe-80a95d155d03"},"sequence":30,"recorded_at":1780531400000055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a14b6b-74d3-7673-9539-63bd290c2683","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"01a14b6b-74d3-7673-9539-63bd290c2683","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a14b6b-74d3-7673-9539-63bd290c2683"},"call_id":"call_01a14b6bf12f7005a553f4c881695d3f","text":"Read text file `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/code-review-package.md`.\n1|# Code Review Package — dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017\n2|\n3|## 1. Metadata & Artifact Hashes\n4|- **Task ID**: `dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017`\n5|- **Jira Issue**: [EYE-33873](https://tasks.sberdevices.ru/browse/EYE-33873)\n6|- **Criticality**: `S2` (`parent_skill=analyst-teamlead`, downstream panel)\n7|- **Architecture Spec**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/architecture/arch-spec.md`\n8|- **Architecture Packet**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/architecture/architecture-packet.json` (`sha256=86de86783a9eaba1d866955443f59cc31da128d715585456898b9590100ed206`)\n9|- **ARCH_PANEL Proof (Round r2)**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/panel/arch/r2/panel-proof.json` (`sha256=564c5afab8e1890222f84bba898f881826f98d4108758eddf2e13a11820d3e69`)\n10|- **Coder Plan**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/plans/coder-01.json` (`sha256=c33259b6f5fdad2d4d99ba138bbeb623e2034a3391895eb09724a45a294e4273`)\n11|- **ADR Document**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/docs/adr/0005-resilient-hub-lifecycle-and-detached-turns.md`\n12|- **Baseline Git Commit**: `d00d698` (`docs(readme): explain official vendor CLIs vs OAuth proxies (CLIProxyAPI)`)\n13|\n14|## 2. Traceability Matrix: Requirements & Arch Decisions (RW-001..RW-010)\n15|| Requirement / Finding | Architecture Decision & Implementation | Implementation Path | Tests |\n16||---|---|---|---|\n17|| **User Directive 1 & RW-001/002**: Detached turn execution on socket drop (`client_gone`) without killing subagent | `ManagedTurn`, `TurnSessionManager`, `TurnBuffer` ring buffer 10MB, `POST/DELETE /v1/turns/<id>/cancel`, `DETACHED_ORPHAN_TTL_S = 300.0` | `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py`, `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n18|| **User Directive 2 & RW-006**: Adaptive idle watchdog (300s) + cputime child monitoring on Darwin + safety cap (3600s) | `AdaptiveTimeoutController`, `ProcessWatchdog` parsing `cputime` across child pgid, fail-closed on `ps` failure | `core/watchdog.py` | `tests/test_adaptive_idle_watchdog.py` |\n19|| **User Directive 3**: Resilience in common hub core layer (`core/`), not per-adapter | Extracted `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `core/watchdog.py`, `core/lifecycle.py`, `core/backend_adapter.py` | `core/` | All test suites |\n20|| **RW-003**: Deterministic turn key | `turn_key = sha256(turn_id:rid:session_id)` prevents collision or reuse across rids | `core/turn_session_manager.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` |\n21|| **RW-004**: Gap Replay detection | Buffer evictions return HTTP 410 `GAP_DETECTED` on reattach with stale `Last-Event-ID` | `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n22|| **RW-005**: Graceful shutdown & drain | `HubLifecycleManager`, non-blocking signal handling via `threading.Event`, drain timeout 110s, 503 `Retry-After: 5` | `core/lifecycle.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_graceful_shutdown_drain.py` |\n23|| **RW-007**: Safe turn disk serialization | Atomic write to `~/.dsh/turns/<id>.json` with schema version 1.0, 0600 file mode, directory 0700 | `core/turn_session_manager.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` |\n24|| **RW-008**: Security input validation | Strict regex `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$` on all `turn_id` path and query params | `server.py`, `bridges/muse-bridge/server.py` | `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n25|| **RW-009**: Feature flags | `DSH_BRIDGE_DETACHED_ENABLED`, `DSH_BRIDGE_WATCHDOG_ENABLED`, `DSH_BRIDGE_DRAIN_ENABLED` defaults | `server.py` | Unit tests |\n26|| **RW-010**: DSH profile syntax fix | Remove invalid `{{cwd}}` from persona-suffix in `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` | `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` | `tests/test_dsh_profile_config.py` |\n27|\n28|## 3. Test Suites & Verification Evidence\n29|- **New Unit Tests** (15 tests, 0.56s execution):\n30|  - `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` (4 tests: detached background finish, reattach streaming, disk persistence, memory buffer)\n31|  - `tests/test_adaptive_idle_watchdog.py` (4 tests: idle reset on tokens, safety cap enforcement, Darwin ps parsing, fail-closed)\n32|  - `tests/test_graceful_shutdown_drain.py` (3 tests: SIGTERM signal event, active turn drain, 503 Retry-After rejection)\n33|  - `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` (3 tests: explicit cancel endpoint, gap 410 detection, orphan TTL reaper)\n34|  - `tests/test_dsh_profile_config.py` (1 test: cordis patch yml validation)\n35|- **Regression Tests**: 208 existing unit and integration tests passing in 122.8s.\n36|- **Code Linter**: `ruff check` passed without any warnings or errors.\n37|\n38|## 4. Full Git Diff (`git diff HEAD`)\n39|```diff\n40|diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\n41|index 32c8f24..f2b7c2b 100644\n42|--- a/README.md\n43|+++ b/README.md\n44|@@ -74,13 +74,13 @@ or script that speaks the OpenAI protocol.\n45| \n46| ## Why official vendor CLIs instead of OAuth proxies (CLIProxyAPI)\n47| \n48|-When direct pay-as-you-go API keys are not used, this hub (`droid exec`, `muse serve`) and its sibling bridges (`claude -p`, `cursor-agent -p`, `agy -p`, `opencode`) spawn the official vendor CLI as a local child process instead of extracting OAuth tokens and calling cloud APIs over raw HTTP like [CLIProxyAPI](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI) (`cliproxy`).\n49|+This hub contains no OAuth handling. It starts the official vendor CLI as a local child process (`droid exec` for the `droid` backend, `muse exec` for the `muse` backend) and returns that CLI's answer through the OpenAI-compatible API. The sibling bridges (`claude -p`, `cursor-agent -p`, `agy -p`, `opencode`) follow the same pattern but live outside this repository. [CLIProxyAPI](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI) (`cliproxy`) takes the other route: it stores OAuth logins for many accounts and sends HTTP requests to provider APIs itself.\n50| \n51| Replaying subscription tokens through an OAuth proxy carries three risks:\n52| \n53|-- **Account bans and subscription revocations.** Providers can ban accounts or revoke subscriptions when OAuth tokens issued to an official vendor CLI are replayed from an external OAuth proxy. Spawning the official vendor CLI avoids HTTP client impersonation, though it does not exempt automated usage from each provider's terms of service or guarantee against policy enforcement.\n54|-- **Anthropic and other official vendor CLIs cannot be faithfully reproduced over HTTP.** As shown in CLIProxyAPI's [utls_transport.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/auth/claude/utls_transport.go) and [claude_executor_cloaking.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/runtime/executor/claude_executor_cloaking.go), mimicking Claude Code (`claude`) over raw HTTP requires custom TLS `ClientHello` fingerprints (`utls`), injected `metadata.user_id` values, salted `x-anthropic-billing-header` hashes (`SHA256(salt + messageText[4,7,20] + version)`), and prompt cloaking of sensitive words.\n55|-- **Server-side detection rules change without notice.** Because client checks are enforced on the provider's servers, rotating the fingerprint salt, checking a new header or telemetry field, or flagging cloaked prompts breaks external OAuth proxies or triggers bans without a client release. The trade-off of the local bridge model is operational: each host must install, authenticate, and update the official vendor CLI binaries.\n56|+- **Account bans and subscription revocations.** Providers can ban accounts or revoke subscriptions when OAuth tokens are replayed from an external proxy. Running the official CLI avoids client impersonation, but it does not make automated use allowed under each provider's terms of service, and it does not guarantee against enforcement.\n57|+- **Client imitation is fragile.** To pass as Claude Code over raw HTTP, CLIProxyAPI copies the client's TLS fingerprint for OAuth requests ([utls_transport.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/auth/claude/utls_transport.go)), injects a fake `metadata.user_id`, computes a 3-character build fingerprint for `x-anthropic-billing-header` from a fixed salt, three sampled prompt characters, and the client version, and obfuscates configured sensitive words in prompts ([claude_executor_cloaking.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/runtime/executor/claude_executor_cloaking.go)). Its code targets specific Claude Code versions, and this was checked for Claude Code only.\n58|+- **Server-side detection rules can change at any time.** Client checks run on the provider's servers. A new salt, header, telemetry field, or prompt check can break an external OAuth proxy or get its accounts flagged, with no new client release. The cost of the local-CLI model is operational: each host must install, sign in to, and update the vendor CLI binaries.\n59| \n60| ## Supported backends and connected agent CLIs\n61| \n62|@@ -111,12 +111,13 @@ documented below and in the [port map](#ecosystem-port-and-architecture-map).\n63| \n64| ### `muse` — Meta Muse CLI (in-tree hub and dedicated bridge)\n65| \n66|-- Transport: `muse serve` (MSP — Muse Server Protocol, JSON-RPC over\n67|+- Transport: headless `muse exec` per turn through the launcher wrapper\n68|+  (`~/.config/muse-launch/muse-cli.sh`). The dedicated `muse-bridge` (port\n69|+  `9886`) uses `muse serve` (MSP — Muse Server Protocol, JSON-RPC over\n70|   stdin/stdout) with `approvalMode: \"allowAll\"` on `session/start`\n71|-  ([ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-muse-serve-approval-allowall.md)), so interactive\n72|-  multi-step sessions run without a turn reset; headless one-shot `muse exec`\n73|-  through a launcher wrapper remains available. Wonder context is pruned\n74|-  (400k/320k/200k) and net-timeouts are retried.\n75|+  ([ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-muse-serve-approval-allowall.md)), so its\n76|+  interactive multi-step sessions run without a turn reset. Wonder context is\n77|+  pruned (400k/320k/200k) and net-timeouts are retried.\n78| - Tool access: Full Access — models can read and write files and run shell\n79|   commands (`--disable-write` / `--disable-shell` are no longer passed).\n80| - Streaming: live `reasoning_content` with the model's thoughts (`summary.*`\n81|@@ -182,7 +183,7 @@ arbitrary code, so a new CLI always lands as explicit, reviewable code plus\n82| | Port | Service / bridge | Backend CLI / engine | Models served | Key characteristics |\n83| |---|---|---|---|---|\n84| | `:9881` | `claude-p-bridge` | `claude -p` | `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5` | Dedicated CLI bridge, tool-calling emulation |\n85|-| `:9882` | `cli-agent-bridge` (hub, this repo) | `droid exec` + `muse serve` | `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `grok-4.7`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `muse-wonder-1.0` | Multi-binary hub, resident sessions, catalog schema 3 |\n86|+| `:9882` | `cli-agent-bridge` (hub, this repo) | `droid exec` + `muse exec` | `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `grok-4.7`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `muse-wonder-1.0` (Muse enabled only) | Multi-binary hub, resident sessions, catalog schema 3 |\n87| | `:9884` | `claude-p-sonnet-bridge` | `claude -p` | `claude-sonnet-5-5` | Dedicated Sonnet 5.5 bridge |\n88| | `:9885` | `grok46-bridge` / `agy-bridge` | `cursor-agent -p` / `agy -p` | `cursor-grok-4.6-high`, `gemini-4-argon` | 500k context, stdin streaming, progressive thinking |\n89| | `:9886` | `muse-bridge` | `muse serve` + `muse exec` | `muse-wonder-1.0`, `muse-spark-1.3` | MSP JSON-RPC, `allowAll` approval, live reasoning |\n90|diff --git a/adapters/droid_adapter.py b/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n91|index b34b485..1f36fbc 100644\n92|--- a/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n93|+++ b/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n94|@@ -80,7 +80,20 @@ class DroidAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n95|         legacy[\"rpc\"][\"items\"] = [asdict(item) for item in ctx.rpc.items]\n96|         legacy[\"images\"] = [asdict(image) for image in ctx.images]\n97|         handler = cast(Any, ctx.handler)\n98|-        raw = handler._run_once(legacy, ctx.keepalive, sse_writer)\n99|+        if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n100|+            ctx.on_activity(\"start\")\n101|+        wrapped_writer: Optional[StreamSink] = None\n102|+        if sse_writer is not None:\n103|+\n104|+            def _wrapped_writer(kind: str, text: str) -> bool:\n105|+                if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n106|+                    ctx.on_activity(kind)\n107|+                return sse_writer(kind, text)\n108|+\n109|+            wrapped_writer = _wrapped_writer\n110|+        raw = handler._run_once(legacy, ctx.keepalive, wrapped_writer)\n111|+        if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n112|+            ctx.on_activity(\"done\")\n113|         usage = raw.get(\"usage\") or {}\n114| \n115|         def tool_call(call: dict) -> ToolCall:\n116|diff --git a/adapters/muse_adapter.py b/adapters/muse_adapter.py\n117|index 3bfd703..ec6da21 100644\n118|--- a/adapters/muse_adapter.py\n119|+++ b/adapters/muse_adapter.py\n120|@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@ from core.backend_adapter import (\n121|     TurnResult,\n122|     Usage,\n123| )\n124|+from core.watchdog import AdaptiveTimeoutController\n125|+\n126| \n127| DEFAULT_WRAPPER = \"~/.config/muse-launch/muse-cli.sh\"\n128| DEFAULT_PROXY_PORT = 10816\n129|@@ -529,10 +531,18 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n130|         waited = self._acquire_slot(ctx)\n131|         if waited:\n132|             return self._result(waited, 1)\n133|+        managed_turn = getattr(ctx.handler, \"_active_managed_turn\", None)\n134|+        if managed_turn is not None:\n135|+            with managed_turn._lock:\n136|+                managed_turn._slot_released = False\n137|+                managed_turn._slot_release_fn = self._slots.release\n138|         try:\n139|             return self._run_exec(ctx, prompt)\n140|         finally:\n141|-            self._slots.release()\n142|+            if managed_turn is not None:\n143|+                managed_turn.release_slot_once()\n144|+            else:\n145|+                self._slots.release()\n146| \n147|     def _run_exec(self, ctx: TurnContext, prompt: str) -> TurnResult:\n148|         model = ctx.model\n149|@@ -565,6 +575,36 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n150|         threads: list[threading.Thread] = []\n151|         state = \"done\"\n152|         timeout_s = self._setting(\"TIMEOUT_S\", 1800.0)\n153|+        cfg_idle = self.config.get(\"idle_timeout_s\")\n154|+        cfg_cap = self.config.get(\"safety_cap_s\")\n155|+        idle_s = (\n156|+            float(cfg_idle)\n157|+            if isinstance(cfg_idle, (int, float)) and not isinstance(cfg_idle, bool)\n158|+            else self._setting(\"IDLE_TIMEOUT_S\", min(300.0, timeout_s))\n159|+        )\n160|+        idle_s = min(idle_s, timeout_s)\n161|+        safety_s = (\n162|+            float(cfg_cap)\n163|+            if isinstance(cfg_cap, (int, float)) and not isinstance(cfg_cap, bool)\n164|+            else self._setting(\"SAFETY_CAP_S\", timeout_s)\n165|+        )\n166|+        if (\n167|+            timeout_s < 300.0\n168|+            and cfg_cap is None\n169|+            and not hasattr(self.host, \"SAFETY_CAP_S\")\n170|+        ):\n171|+            safety_s = timeout_s\n172|+        watchdog_enabled = os.environ.get(\n173|+            \"BRIDGE_ADAPTIVE_WATCHDOG_ENABLED\", \"true\"\n174|+        ).strip().lower() in (\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\")\n175|+        timeout_ctrl = AdaptiveTimeoutController(\n176|+            idle_timeout_s=idle_s,\n177|+            safety_cap_s=safety_s,\n178|+            finish_reserve_s=0.0 if safety_s <= 60.0 else 35.0,\n179|+            watchdog_enabled=watchdog_enabled,\n180|+            turn_id=ctx.turn_id,\n181|+            log_fn=self._log,\n182|+        )\n183|         pipe_fds: list[int] = []\n184|         try:\n185|             try:\n186|@@ -600,15 +640,19 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n187|                 raise OSError(\"group witness handshake timed out\")\n188|             member = int(os.read(ready_r, 32).strip())\n189|             self._register_child(proc.pid, member)\n190|+            if callable(ctx.register_pgid):\n191|+                ctx.register_pgid(proc.pid)\n192|             os.write(gate_w, b\"1\")\n193|             for fd in (ready_r, gate_w):\n194|                 os.close(fd)\n195|                 pipe_fds.remove(fd)\n196|             if self._shutting_down:  # shutdown успел пройти до регистрации ребёнка\n197|                 self._kill_group(proc)\n198|-            keepalive_s = self._setting(\"KEEPALIVE_S\", 15.0)\n199|+            keepalive_s = min(10.0, self._setting(\"KEEPALIVE_S\", 10.0))\n200|             gone = ctx.client_gone\n201|             keepalive = ctx.keepalive\n202|+            cancel_ev = ctx.cancel_event\n203|+            detach_ok = bool(ctx.detach_on_disconnect)\n204|             stdout, stderr = proc.stdout, proc.stderr\n205|             assert stdout is not None and stderr is not None\n206|             child = proc\n207|@@ -617,24 +661,51 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n208|             leader_exited: list[float] = []\n209| \n210|             def watch() -> None:\n211|-                deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout_s\n212|                 last_ka = time.monotonic()\n213|+                seeded = False\n214|+                detached = False\n215|                 while not done.wait(0.25):\n216|                     now = time.monotonic()\n217|+                    if not seeded:\n218|+                        seeded = True\n219|+                        timeout_ctrl.register_pgid(child.pid)\n220|+                    if cancel_ev is not None and cancel_ev.is_set():\n221|+                        flags[\"cancelled\"] = True\n222|+                        self._kill_group(child)\n223|+                        return\n224|                     if child.poll() is not None:\n225|                         if not leader_exited:\n226|                             leader_exited.append(now)\n227|                         if now - leader_exited[0] >= STDERR_DRAIN_GRACE_S:\n228|                             self._kill_group(child)\n229|                             return\n230|-                    elif now > deadline:\n231|-                        flags[\"timeout\"] = True\n232|-                    elif callable(gone) and gone():\n233|-                        flags[\"client_gone\"] = True\n234|-                    elif callable(keepalive) and now - last_ka >= keepalive_s:\n235|-                        last_ka = now\n236|-                        if not keepalive():\n237|-                            flags[\"client_gone\"] = True\n238|+                    else:\n239|+                        should_stop, wd_reason, _ = timeout_ctrl.check(child.pid)\n240|+                        if should_stop and wd_reason in (\n241|+                            \"idle_timeout\",\n242|+                            \"absolute_cap\",\n243|+                        ):\n244|+                            flags[\"timeout\"] = True\n245|+                        elif not detached and callable(gone) and gone():\n246|+                            if detach_ok:\n247|+                                detached = True\n248|+                                if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n249|+                                    ctx.on_activity(\"detached\")\n250|+                            else:\n251|+                                flags[\"client_gone\"] = True\n252|+                        elif (\n253|+                            not detached\n254|+                            and callable(keepalive)\n255|+                            and now - last_ka >= keepalive_s\n256|+                        ):\n257|+                            last_ka = now\n258|+                            if not keepalive():\n259|+                                if detach_ok:\n260|+                                    detached = True\n261|+                                    if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n262|+                                        ctx.on_activity(\"detached\")\n263|+                                else:\n264|+                                    flags[\"client_gone\"] = True\n265|                     if flags:\n266|                         self._kill_group(child)\n267|                         return\n268|@@ -705,6 +776,9 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n269|                     line = bytes(pending[:size]).decode(\"utf-8\", \"strict\")\n270|                     del pending[:size]\n271|                     events.feed_line(line)\n272|+                    timeout_ctrl.record_activity(\"protocol\")\n273|+                    if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n274|+                        ctx.on_activity(\"protocol\")\n275|                     if events.text_bytes > MAX_TURN_TEXT_BYTES:\n276|                         raise ValueError(\"turn text exceeds the limit\")\n277|                 if len(pending) > MAX_LINE_BYTES:\n278|@@ -724,6 +798,7 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n279|                 f\"muse pump failed: {type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)[:MAX_ERR_CHARS]}\"\n280|             )\n281|         finally:\n282|+            timeout_ctrl.close()\n283|             if proc is not None:\n284|                 # Владение начинается сразу после Popen: даже отказ первого Thread.start\n285|                 # не может обойти kill/wait. Реестр и слот освобождаются ПОСЛЕ группы.\n286|@@ -756,6 +831,8 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n287|         err = \"\\n\".join(events.errors + err_lines)[-1000:]\n288|         if events.reason:\n289|             err = (err + f\"\\nreason: {events.reason}\").strip()\n290|+        if flags.get(\"cancelled\"):\n291|+            return self._result(\"cancelled\", 1, err=\"turn cancelled by user\")\n292|         if flags.get(\"client_gone\"):\n293|             return self._result(\"client_gone\", 1)\n294|         if flags.get(\"timeout\"):\n295|@@ -779,6 +856,7 @@ class MuseAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n296|             return self._result(\"backend_error\", rc, err=err)\n297|         return self._result(\"done\", 0, text=events.text, err=err, prompt=prompt)\n298| \n299|+\n300|     def shutdown(self) -> None:\n301|         \"\"\"Убить группы процессов собственных детей (только свои PID из реестра адаптера).\"\"\"\n302|         self._shutting_down = True\n303|diff --git a/bridges/muse-bridge/server.py b/bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\n304|index 2b010b5..ff19017 100644\n305|--- a/bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\n306|+++ b/bridges/muse-bridge/server.py\n307|@@ -57,13 +57,27 @@ from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n308| from pathlib import Path\n309| from typing import Any, NamedTuple\n310| \n311|+_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n312|+if str(_REPO_ROOT) not in sys.path:\n313|+    sys.path.insert(0, str(_REPO_ROOT))\n314|+\n315|+from core.backend_adapter import ToolCall, TurnResult, Usage  # noqa: E402\n316|+from core.lifecycle import HubLifecycleManager  # noqa: E402\n317|+from core.turn_session_manager import (  # noqa: E402\n318|+    GapDetectedError,\n319|+    ManagedTurn,\n320|+    TurnSessionManager,\n321|+    validate_turn_id,\n322|+)\n323|+\n324| logger = logging.getLogger(\"muse-bridge\")\n325| \n326| HOST = os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\").strip() or \"127.0.0.1\"\n327| PORT = int(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_PORT\", \"9886\"))\n328| AUTH_KEY = os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_KEY\", \"\").strip()\n329| \n330|-TIMEOUT_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_S\", \"1800\"))\n331|+TIMEOUT_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT_S\", \"3600\"))\n332|+IDLE_TIMEOUT_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S\", \"300\"))\n333| MAX_CONCURRENT = int(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_MAX_CONCURRENT\", \"2\"))\n334| \n335| MUSE_WRAPPER = os.environ.get(\n336|@@ -145,7 +159,7 @@ TRANSIENT_RETRY_SCOPE = os.environ.get(\n337| ).strip()\n338| FINISH_RESERVE_S = 35.0\n339| CLOSE_RESERVE_S = 12.0\n340|-REQUEST_CAP_S = 1800.0\n341|+REQUEST_CAP_S = 3600.0\n342| MIN_ATTEMPT_REMAINING_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_MIN_ATTEMPT_S\", \"120\"))\n343| CONTROL_WRITE_TIMEOUT_S = 5.0\n344| LIVE_WRITE_TIMEOUT_S = 3.0\n345|@@ -364,11 +378,54 @@ def _log(msg: str) -> None:\n346|         pass\n347| \n348| \n349|-def _auth_ok(handler: BaseHTTPRequestHandler) -> bool:\n350|-    hdr = handler.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n351|+def _is_detached_enabled() -> bool:\n352|+    return os.environ.get(\"BRIDGE_ENABLE_DETACHED_TURNS\", \"1\") not in (\n353|+        \"0\",\n354|+        \"false\",\n355|+        \"False\",\n356|+    )\n357|+\n358|+\n359|+def _is_watchdog_enabled() -> bool:\n360|+    return os.environ.get(\"BRIDGE_ENABLE_ADAPTIVE_WATCHDOG\", \"1\") not in (\n361|+        \"0\",\n362|+        \"false\",\n363|+        \"False\",\n364|+    )\n365|+\n366|+\n367|+def _is_drain_enabled() -> bool:\n368|+    return os.environ.get(\"BRIDGE_ENABLE_GRACEFUL_DRAIN\", \"1\") not in (\n369|+        \"0\",\n370|+        \"false\",\n371|+        \"False\",\n372|+    )\n373|+\n374|+\n375|+def _extract_auth_token(handler: BaseHTTPRequestHandler) -> str:\n376|+    hdrs = getattr(handler, \"headers\", None) or {}\n377|+    hdr = hdrs.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n378|     if hdr.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n379|-        return hdr[7:].strip() == AUTH_KEY\n380|-    return handler.headers.get(\"x-api-key\", \"\") == AUTH_KEY or hdr.strip() == AUTH_KEY\n381|+        return hdr[7:].strip()\n382|+    return hdrs.get(\"x-api-key\", \"\") or hdr.strip()\n383|+\n384|+\n385|+def _auth_ok(handler: BaseHTTPRequestHandler) -> bool:\n386|+    return _extract_auth_token(handler) == AUTH_KEY\n387|+\n388|+\n389|+def _owner_token_hash(handler: BaseHTTPRequestHandler) -> str:\n390|+    tok = _extract_auth_token(handler) or AUTH_KEY or \"anon\"\n391|+    return hashlib.sha256(tok.encode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")).hexdigest()\n392|+\n393|+\n394|+TURN_MANAGER = TurnSessionManager(state_root=WORKSPACE / \"turns\", log_fn=_log)\n395|+LIFECYCLE = HubLifecycleManager(turn_manager=TURN_MANAGER, log_fn=_log)\n396|+\n397|+\n398|+def _reset_state() -> None:\n399|+    TURN_MANAGER.reset()\n400|+    LIFECYCLE.reset_for_tests()\n401| \n402| \n403| def _redact_secrets(text: str) -> str:\n404|@@ -1365,7 +1422,7 @@ SSE_CHUNK_DELAY_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_SSE_CHUNK_DELAY_S\", \"0.005\n405| # stream=true: заголовки и role-кадр уходят сразу, пока ход идёт — комментарии keepalive.\n406| # Без них клиент (OpenAI SDK в DeepSeek Harness) ждал заголовков до своего таймаута\n407| # (~600 с) и рвал долгий ход как \"Request timed out\".\n408|-KEEPALIVE_S = float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_KEEPALIVE_S\", \"15\"))\n409|+KEEPALIVE_S = min(10.0, float(os.environ.get(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_KEEPALIVE_S\", \"10\")))\n410| \n411| \n412| def _split_sse_chunks(text: str, size: int = 0) -> list[str]:\n413|@@ -1532,6 +1589,7 @@ class Run:\n414|         self.approval_seen = False\n415|         self.observed_barrier = False\n416|         self.exec_deadline = float(\"inf\")\n417|+        self.managed_turn: ManagedTurn | None = None\n418| \n419|     def close(self) -> None:\n420|         \"\"\"Убить группу процессов хода и коротко дождаться её ухода.\n421|@@ -1637,6 +1695,13 @@ class Run:\n422|                     \"err\": f\"spawn failed: {exc}\",\n423|                     \"state\": \"spawn_failed\",\n424|                 }\n425|+            if self.managed_turn is not None:\n426|+                self.managed_turn.bind_process(\n427|+                    pgid=self.proc.pid, terminate_fn=self.close\n428|+                )\n429|+                TURN_MANAGER.register_child_pgid(\n430|+                    self.proc.pid, backend=\"muse\", turn_id=self.managed_turn.turn_id\n431|+                )\n432|             self.action_possible = True\n433| \n434|             def drain_stderr() -> None:\n435|@@ -1674,6 +1739,8 @@ class Run:\n436|                         continue\n437|                     if not isinstance(event, dict):\n438|                         continue\n439|+                    if self.managed_turn is not None:\n440|+                        self.managed_turn.touch_activity(\"protocol\")\n441|                     ptype = str(event.get(\"payload_type\") or \"\")\n442|                     raw_payload = event.get(\"payload\")\n443|                     payload: dict[str, Any] = (\n444|@@ -1822,6 +1889,7 @@ class ServeRun:\n445|         self.request_deadline = float(\"inf\")\n446|         self.turn_started_at: float | None = None\n447|         self._live_frozen = False\n448|+        self.managed_turn: ManagedTurn | None = None\n449|         # Сквозной live-стриминг всех шагов (ADR-0004): аккумулятор по\n450|         # составному ключу (item_id, idx), единый append-only stream-текст\n451|         # для live/final/flush (S2), доступ — только под _acc_lock (S3).\n452|@@ -2014,6 +2082,13 @@ class ServeRun:\n453|         except OSError as exc:\n454|             raise ServeUnavailable(f\"serve spawn failed: {exc}\")\n455|         assert self.proc.stdout is not None and self.proc.stdin is not None\n456|+        if self.managed_turn is not None:\n457|+            self.managed_turn.bind_process(\n458|+                pgid=self.proc.pid, terminate_fn=self.close\n459|+            )\n460|+            TURN_MANAGER.register_child_pgid(\n461|+                self.proc.pid, backend=\"muse\", turn_id=self.managed_turn.turn_id\n462|+            )\n463|         # stdin неблокирующий: запись идёт срезами с дедлайном (см. _send).\n464|         os.set_blocking(self.proc.stdin.fileno(), False)\n465| \n466|@@ -2051,6 +2126,9 @@ class ServeRun:\n467| \n468|         def read_msg(timeout_at: float) -> dict[str, Any]:\n469|             while time.monotonic() < timeout_at:\n470|+                if self.managed_turn is not None and self.managed_turn.cancel_event.is_set():\n471|+                    self.close()\n472|+                    raise ServeUnavailable(\"turn cancelled\")\n473|                 if self.proc is None or self.proc.stdout is None:\n474|                     raise ServeUnavailable(\"serve stdout closed\")\n475|                 newline = rbuf.find(b\"\\n\")\n476|@@ -2083,6 +2161,8 @@ class ServeRun:\n477|                 except ValueError:\n478|                     continue\n479|                 if isinstance(msg, dict):\n480|+                    if self.managed_turn is not None:\n481|+                        self.managed_turn.touch_activity(\"protocol\")\n482|                     return msg\n483|             raise ServeUnavailable(\"serve read timeout\")\n484| \n485|@@ -2643,6 +2723,8 @@ class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n486|     # Обрыв клиента и текущий ход: значения инициализируются в setup() каждого соединения.\n487|     _client_gone: bool = False\n488|     _current_run: Run | ServeRun | None = None\n489|+    _active_managed_turn: ManagedTurn | None = None\n490|+    _detach_on_disconnect: bool = False\n491|     # Ранний SSE (stream=true): состояние потока и keepalive текущего соединения.\n492|     _sse_open: bool = False\n493|     _content_started: bool = False\n494|@@ -2669,6 +2751,8 @@ class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n495|         # Состояние обрыва клиента и ссылка на текущий ход — на каждое соединение.\n496|         self._client_gone = False\n497|         self._current_run = None\n498|+        self._active_managed_turn = None\n499|+        self._detach_on_disconnect = False\n500|         self._sse_open = False\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
